        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ba71a60f-17b5-5ab3-8572-d412868405ec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Gelatine airship\n- Organizations: United States Army Signal Corps\n- People: Lincoln J. Beachey\n- Places: Portland, Oregon; Guild's Lake; Vancouver, Washington; Vancouver Barracks\n- Events: Lewis and Clark Centennial Exposition\n\nFacts:\n- Lincoln J. Beachey was born on March 3, 1887, and he became a pioneer American aviator and barnstormer.\n- Gelatine was an airship operated by the United States Army Signal Corps.\n- On the morning of September 19, 1905, Lincoln J. Beachey piloted the airship Gelatine from the grounds of the Lewis and Clark Centennial Exposition on the shores of Guild's Lake in Portland, Oregon.\n- Gelatine landed 40 minutes later at the Vancouver Barracks in Vancouver, Washington.\n- Lincoln J. Beachey died on March 14, 1915.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
